refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public boolReflectionProperty::isWritable stringnullscope objectnullobject&null;
Checks whether writing to the property from the given scope would be allowed. The visibility of the property, including its asymmetric visibility, its hooks, the __set() magic method and, if an object is given, the state of a readonly property on that object are taken into account.
A return value of &true; does not guarantee that writing to the property succeeds. For example, a set hook or __set() may still throw an exception, and the type of the assigned value is not considered.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns &false; if the visibility or set visibility of the property does not allow writing from scope, if it is a virtual property without a set hook, or if object is given and the readonly property is already initialized on it. Otherwise &true; is returned.
However, if the class defines __set(), &true; is returned for a non-static property that is not visible from scope.

&reftitle.errors;
Throws a ReflectionException if object is given for a static property, or if object is not an instance of the class the property was declared in.
Throws an Error if scope is not the name of an existing class.

  &reftitle.examples;

   ReflectionProperty::isWritable example


<?php
class User
{
    public readonly string $name;

    public function setName(string $name): void
    {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}

$reflectionProperty = new ReflectionProperty(User::class, 'name');
$user = new User();

// Readonly properties can only be written from inside the class
var_dump($reflectionProperty->isWritable(null, $user));

// The property is not initialized yet
var_dump($reflectionProperty->isWritable(User::class, $user));

$user->setName('Alice');
var_dump($reflectionProperty->isWritable(User::class, $user));

// Without an object, only the declaration of the property is considered
var_dump($reflectionProperty->isWritable(User::class));


   &example.outputs;


bool(false)
bool(true)
bool(false)
bool(true)
